summary:
- topic: Meeting Opening & Agenda Amendment
  text: The meeting was called to order, roll call was taken, and the agenda was amended
    to include a public comment period.
- topic: Chair's Apology & Thanks
  text: The Chair offered a public apology for her conduct at the previous meeting
    and thanked the student board members for their dedication.
- topic: Upcoming Key Dates
  text: Dates were announced for a public workshop with the superintendent search
    firm (Zeal) on December 22nd and a community forum on January 22nd.
- topic: FY2027 Budget Presentation
  text: Assistant Superintendent Prince presented an overview of the FY2027 budget
    development, including district demographics, financial context, and various tax
    increase options.
- topic: Demographics & Staffing
  text: The presentation highlighted declining enrollment, increased special education
    and multilingual learner populations, and changes in staff composition and student-to-staff
    ratios over the last decade.
- topic: Budget Forecast & Per-Pupil Spending
  text: The board reviewed a budget forecast showing potential tax increases ranging
    from 3.1% (flat spending) to 17.1% (maintaining current services), noting South
    Portland's higher per-pupil spending compared to some neighboring districts.
- topic: Ideas for Financial Sustainability
  text: 'Four ''big ideas'' for long-term financial sustainability were introduced:
    elementary school grade level reconfiguration, a single middle school start time,
    high school/adult education programming redesign, and service unit operational
    efficiencies.'
- topic: Board Guidance & Public Comment
  text: Board members provided initial guidance for the FY2027 budget, generally aiming
    for a tax increase between Option A (3.1%) and Option B (9.7%), with 6.5% suggested
    as a starting point. Public comment included calls for more detailed financial
    data and concerns about the impact of cuts on staff and students.
